<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.African money market shortage rises further.</title>
<headline>S.African money market shortage rises further.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's money market shortage rose to 8.722 billion rand on Tuesday from 8.359 billion on Monday, according to latest Reserve Bank figures.</p>
<p>On the money market on Wednesday, three-month NCD rates rose to between 16.30 and 16.20 percent from 16.30 to 16.15 percent on Tuesday. The 90-day BA rate was also higher at 15.70 to 15.60 percent from  15.70 to 15.55 percent.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
